From 23c6b8ff1c86698b789d1eab5ae8b6700371036a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David <david@katalystnord.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 18:59:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] kv-stream: LLAMA_KV_SPLIT=auto, the CPU's share found by
 measuring; LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_NOOP

Beast's tuner: from share 0 a step of 0.1 is kept when decode steps get at least
2% faster (windows of 16 steps, the first two after a change skipped, steps
slower than three times the median left out); it settles and looks again after
512 steps or when the streamed part changes by a quarter. Nothing splits while
nothing streams. Two changes for this fork:
- the resident binding is rebuilt at every KV layout change (about every 60
  tokens at 130K), so the tuner state lives outside it;
- from 0, when 0.1 does not pay, 0.2 is tried once: a small share does not cover
  the split's fixed cost (130K: 113.1 ms per token at 0, 111.7 at 0.1, 103.6 at
  0.2).

130K: settles at 0.3 to 0.5 (8.55 -> 9.5 t/s over 256 tokens); 64K without
streaming: never splits. LLAMA_KV_SPLIT_NOOP (measuring only, output wrong) skips
the CPU's part to show the most the split could give.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
